  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 118 PM CDT Tue Jun 16 2026\n\nFor Thursday, the combination of hot temperatures and high \nhumidity values will make it the worst day for the heat wave. The\nafternoon heat index values will be 105 to 110 again, possibly up\nto 112 across the Heartland and Northwest Hill Country. Also, \nhighs will be 105 to 110 across much of the area. A Heat Advisory \nis in effect for Thursday. Also, very little cooling for Wednesday\nnight as lows will be in the mid 70s to lower 80s Thursday \nmorning.\n\nAn unsettled weather pattern and slightly cooler temperatures return \nlate this week and weekend with scattered mainly afternoon and \nevening thunderstorms. There is a marginal risk of severe weather \nacross the northern half of the area Thursday night as a cold front \nmoves south. Also, there is marginal to slight risk of excessive \nrainfall on Friday with localized flash flooding possible. Going \nwith mainly a dry forecast early next week with highs around 100 \nagain.",
